      "side": 1,
      "message": "unfortunately, we get back all the DNs that have a role assignment. The DN can be the DN for a user or a group. get_role_assignments isn\u0027t smart enough to get only user DNs and it sticks all of them in user_dn. Here\u0027s an example run: http://paste.openstack.org/show/81018/\n\n (Pdb) pp [x.user_dn for x in assignments]\n [u\u0027cn\u003d0ddcdc2ee75246999f662a1b09853086,ou\u003dUsers,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg\u0027,\n  u\u0027cn\u003d0ddcdc2ee75246999f662a1b09853086,ou\u003dUsers,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg\u0027,\n  u\u0027cn\u003d73114eaf976e4f6480776c3d49213289,ou\u003dUsers,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg\u0027,\n  u\u0027cn\u003dsuspectid,ou\u003dUserGroups,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg\u0027,\n  u\u0027cn\u003d0ddcdc2ee75246999f662a1b09853086,ou\u003dUsers,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg\u0027]\n\nSo you can see cn\u003dsuspectid,ou\u003dUserGroups,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg (which is obviously a group) is in the list of user_dns.\n\nThe issue that\u0027s being fixed here is that a user and group have the same ID. So there could be a user with ID suspectid (cn\u003dsuspectid,ou\u003dUsers,dc\u003dopenstack,dc\u003dorg) also.\n\nSo just checking the ID at line 100 isn\u0027t good enough, because the user ID might be a group ID instead.",
